Anzu is a small, light bird-like man (a tengu) with feathers and a beak, and a member of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He is well-studied in occult and religious matters and is the Party's reader of magic: he identifies what they find, names the creatures they meet, and works out their riddles. He keeps the raven [[People/Othello|Othello]], and carries a staff of light wood he made himself, with a perch for Othello and a dusting of black and blue dots that seem to move when stared at.

He comes from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], where much of his family is connected to [[Belvedere]]. His father is [[People/Adal|Adal]]. His sister [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] went missing after months spent with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]], and he has said he does not want to fight her.

He heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], and it is the center of his work. He believes the power it gave him came for a reason: that he sees the danger coming and will save people from it. When he draws on the song he sees his arms come apart into tentacles and mouths. After months of study he concluded that the song lives only in the heads of those who hear it, and he made a sheet of music that hangs a little out of the world, pulled toward the void.

He was the only survivor of the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and he took his revenge: he killed the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] and the gang's leader [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. He travels with [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]], [[People/Benny|Benny]], [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]]. Unlike them, he carries no mark of [[Aut]].
